Package: AgriDesign
Title: Design and Analysis of Agricultural Experiments
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Luis Ángel", "Barrera-Guzmán", , "lbarrerag@chapingo.mx", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-8057-2583"))
Description: Plans and analyses agricultural experiments with classical
    designs: completely randomised, randomised complete blocks (also
    generalised), Latin, Graeco-Latin and Youden squares, balanced,
    cyclic, alpha and lattice incomplete blocks, augmented designs,
    factorials, split-plots, strip-plots, split-split-plots and nested
    designs, with or without covariates. Each analysis of variance tests
    every term against its own error stratum; least-squares means are
    separated with eleven multiple-comparison procedures and compact
    letters, with simple effects, trends and contrasts. It checks the
    assumptions, offers transformations and rank-based alternatives,
    recovers inter-block information by restricted maximum likelihood,
    randomises field layouts with field books and power calculations,
    draws publication figures and writes HTML reports. It also includes
    plant breeding analyses (AMMI, stability, line x tester, diallel and
    North Carolina designs) and plant pathology tools (area under the
    disease progress curve, soil heterogeneity). Only base R is used.
